# The memory guard against one long task (cavekit-device-headroom.md R1, cavekit-eaglercraft.md R6, T-672):
# jihad-memhog.html takes 750 MB at 12 MB a second in ONE task, as EaglercraftX's start took 621 MB with the device's
# free memory at 30-40 MB and the GPU hung until a reboot. The guard's thread (every 2 s, whatever the main thread does)
# sees this daemon past half the RAM with MemFree under 64 MB, stops the running script (engine patch 0124), and the
# pump's guard then stops the page (about:stopped, with the page's address and its "Try it again" link). The device stays itself: no GPU fault in the kernel's log, and the
# card loads a page again. The card starts on a plain page and opens the hog after the log's mark: started on the hog, its
# one task held the card's first frames until the guard had already acted (Mochi, 2026-11-19).
id: memory-guard-task
section: The engine
item: A page that takes memory in one long task is stopped by the memory guard before the device runs out: its script ended, the page stopped, no GPU fault, the card usable after
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-colors.html
kit: cavekit-device-headroom.md R1
mark
launch http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-memhog.html?mb=750&rate=12&task=1 60
wait line 'memory guard .thread.: this daemon' 300
wait line 'the running content script stopped' 10
wait line 'memory shed: a page stopped' 30
wait url about:stopped 20
wait rect 'sel:#link' 10
expect text-has 'sel:#where' jihad-memhog.html
expect gpu-calm
launch http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-colors.html
